column4:
In 2022 Open Data Progress and Impact Assessment survey‘s results showed that open data created impact on environmental challenges - 40 % respondents from 165 state and municipal institutions and bodies (please look at the chart No. 14,  https://data.gov.lt/news/30)

==Original==


1.	Portal “Tvarkau miestą” (https://tvarkaumiesta.lt/)  allows users to inform the relevant city municipality about problems in the city (abandoned cars, garbage, lighting, etc.)/ The portal uses and shows data for 8 cities on real time. 
2.	Unified information system for accounting for products, packaging and waste – GPAIS (https://www.gpais.eu/web/guest) .GPAIS is dedicated to the collection, analysis and control of product, packaging and waste (GPA) accounting data. With its help, accounting of waste generation, management, supply of products and packaging to the domestic market is carried out, and other GPA accounting data is processed. In addition, GPAIS is a directory of manufacturers and importers. GPAIS functions include reporting and other document submission, report verification, data analysis and processing, and other processes.
3.	Datasets on different domains can be found on our national data portal, here are some examples classified by topics: 
Energy datasets - https://data.gov.lt/datasets?category_id=62; 
environment datsets - https://data.gov.lt/datasets?category_id=1;
transport datasets - https://data.gov.lt/datasets?category_id=161;
regions and cities - https://data.gov.lt/datasets?category_id=244.
